<title>USA: AutoLend says derivative settlement closed.</title>
<headline>AutoLend says derivative settlement closed.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI BEACH, Fla. 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>AutoLend Group Inc said on Wednesday the settlement of derivative claims in Delaware Court of Chancery had been closed.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the principal terms of the settlement contemplated the sale of the AutoLend IAP subsidiary to an affiliate of Steve Simon, who resigned as chief executive. He was succeeded by Nunzio DeSantis.</p>
<p>&quot;We are extremely pleased that the closing of the settlement will allow AutoLend to focus its energies on moving forward and developing in new directions,&quot; DeSantis said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsroom, (212) 859-1610</p>
